From ee42f9b2e9e3638144e1c2d61d6d5fb831e6064c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:30:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pick): refuse face-normal alignment on an inside-out or
 open body

Face outward normals for the plane lay (one face or two edges) and the
3-2-1 work-offset alignment came from the facets' winding with no check
that the winding is the solid's outside: an inside-out STL laid the part
upside down silently. pick::winding now judges each body (connected
facets over welded edges, 1e-4 mm spatial-hash weld): closed and
consistently wound with positive signed volume (divergence theorem) is
trusted; inside-out, open, non-manifold, mixed-winding or zero-volume
bodies refuse the pick by face and part name. Nothing mutates the
user's geometry. Verdicts are memoized in a bounded thread-local MRU
keyed by an ordered, winding-sensitive content hash.

Pinned by winding_align (inverted cube refuses the face lay, the
two-edge lay and the 3-2-1; the outward cube still aligns; open,
mixed and non-manifold bodies refuse; bodies judged one by one; the
shipped test models read outward; testdata/models/cube_inside_out.stl
reads inside-out).

Fixes #366

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
